<h2 id="ha-ctrl-015-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Exercise a timestamped snapshot, unknown capture time, loading stream, playable stream, stalled stream and denied access. No stale image may retain an unsupported Live claim.
2. Compare entity Idle/Streaming/Recording where supplied with the actual viewer state. Do not infer recording solely from a feed or absence from Idle.
3. Test keyboard playback/fullscreen/exit, focus return, control contrast on varied frames and supported motion/audio controls. Record missing alternatives honestly.
4. Review shared-display content and public evidence for real faces, addresses, tokens and private URLs. Verify that retry or closing the viewer does not secretly change camera privacy or recording settings.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

